homehub third-party notices
===========================

homehub is pure Python (3.10+) and uses only the standard library. It bundles and vendors no
third-party code, so no third-party license texts ship with it. scripts/license-check.py enforces this in CI.

External programs homehub can CALL, but does not include. They are installed separately by you
(or by install.sh only when you ask), each under its own license:

| Program | Used by | License | How it is obtained |
|---|---|---|---|
| dish-monitor v0.1.0 (github.com/jasondmillwood/dish-monitor) | starlink module | MIT | optional; install.sh --with-dish-monitor downloads its installer (sha256-pinned) |
| smartmontools (smartctl) | drives module, scripts/root | GPL-2.0-or-later | your distribution's package manager; run as a separate program |
| LibreSpeed speedtest-cli 1.0.14 | speedtest module (default) | LGPL-3.0 | optional download from its GitHub releases, sha256-pinned; unmodified binary |
| Ookla Speedtest CLI 1.2.0 | speedtest module (alternative) | Proprietary (Ookla EULA) | only after you accept Ookla's license and privacy terms interactively; never redistributed |
| NVIDIA nvidia-smi | gpu module | NVIDIA driver license | part of your NVIDIA driver |
| Folding@home client v8 | gpu module (optional) | GPL-3.0 | from foldingathome.org; homehub only reads its local WebSocket |
| ntfy (ntfy.sh or self-hosted) | alerts module | Apache-2.0 / GPL-2.0 (server) | network service; homehub sends HTTP POSTs |
| xAI API (api.x.ai) | explain module (off by default) | xAI terms of service | network service; requires your own API key |
| curl | install.sh, helper scripts | curl license (MIT-style) | your distribution |
